<title>USA: Triton says Colombia fields at 185,000 bpd.</title>
<headline>Triton says Colombia fields at 185,000 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triton Energy Corp said Thursday that it was making progress in bringing up Colombia's giant Cusiana and Cupiagua oil fields to the 500,000 barrel per day (bpd) target.</p>
<p>&quot;The fields are producing 185,000 bpd, the highest average daily rate in any quarterly financial period to date,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
